// TEST: Caret Rank-0 Reduce Rejected (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3001
// ERROR-CONTAINS: rank mismatch
// ============================================================================
// The boundary of 047. Teaching the array synthesis to read the caret must NOT
// teach it to invent a rank where none was claimed: `T^0` (equivalently a bare
// `T`) records NO arity constraint -- `LookupOrCreateTypeVar` only writes one
// for `arity > 0` -- so `reduce` keeps its rank-1 default for it, exactly as
// before.
//
// The consequence is visible at the CALL, and that is the point: the parameter
// is a rank-1 array demand, so passing a scalar is refused with the rank
// mismatch, instead of a rank-0 fold being silently invented for a value that
// has no axis to fold. A call site neither broadcasts nor reduces rank
// (arity/042's rule); reading the caret adds no exception for folds.
// ============================================================================
function total(x: T^0) -> Float64 = reduce(x, (+))

let s = total(3.0)
